=begin
      author: Fizzleworth
        name: mdemon_refresh
        game: gemstone
        tags: sorcerer, demon, minor summoning
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.7
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Keeps a Sorcerer's Minor Summoning (725) demon refreshed.

  Watches the Minor Summoning spell duration. When it drops below the configured
  buffer, it stows whatever's in your left hand (if anything), rummages a vakra
  runestone out of your kit, rubs it to refresh the demon, puts the runestone
  away, then gets your original left-hand item back.

  If no vakra runestone is found in your kit, the script needs fizzfuse to make a
  new one -- which will pull you away from the hunt (bank + alchemist trip). How
  that's handled is controlled by AUTO_FUSE_RUNESTONE below:
    true  - automatically runs fizzfuse to fuse a new vakra runestone, but with
            FUSE_ONLY_WHEN_RESTING_IN_TOWN (default) only once you're sitting in
            town with nothing hostile around; until then it just waits. bigshot
            is paused while fizzfuse walks.
    false - pauses and waits for you to type "nod" before fusing, so it never
            interrupts a hunt without your say-so.

  Usage:  ;mdemon_refresh
  Stop:   ;kill mdemon_refresh

  Also, once per rest (sitting, mana >= SEND_MANA_AT, nothing hostile around), it
  sends the demon the mana it can hold (;demonmana send); attack-ultima / sac4mana
  ask for it back with ;demonmana get the first time mana runs low in a hunt.

  If it's still "on its way" after TOWN_ON_AFTER_MINUTES and you're in Wehnimer's Landing, Icemule
  or Mist Harbor (where minor demons are legal), it says TELL MDEMON TO TOWN ON, once per demon:
  with TOWN OFF a demon with no illusion won't walk into a town by itself, only while following
  you (11/04-05: a grantris left behind in Landing never came back). If it's still on its way
  after STUCK_WARN_MINUTES, it says so once and suggests ;summond to replace it.

  Calls the demon back (11/04, after it was left behind once more -- in the Rift's swim
  home): while Minor Summoning is up and the demon isn't in the room, it sends a silent
  `tell mdemon return` every CALL_GAP_SECONDS. The reply names the demon, so the script
  learns its id and stops asking while it is standing there. "The magic in your location
  is interfering with your <demon> returning to you" slows the asking to every
  CALL_BLOCKED_GAP_SECONDS, but only while you stay in that room (11/07: the slow-down used to
  outlast the room -- the bank teller blocked it, the 90 s ran on after the walk back to the
  inn, and the raven stood outside the gemcutter's for 80 s until Scott ordered it by hand).
  A real order is echoed with how the trip is going; the silent "already here" replies are not.
  The game gives no ETA (gswiki lists no locate/status command either; "begins to travel" and
  "arrives" are all it says), so the line is a clock: every order for the first minute, then one
  a minute, says how many seconds and orders the trip has taken and what is normal
  (normal_trip_seconds); past slow_trip_seconds it says the trip is slow. While the demon is away
  the script looks for it every second and says "back after N s (M orders)" the moment it shows
  up. (11/20 raven logs: median trip 13 s, but some stalled for minutes: 27 orders / 408 s twice,
  40 orders / 608 s four times.)
  It also keeps a record of the rooms where the demon is slow (Scott 11/20): the wait is
  counted in the room you are standing in (from the first order, or from when you walked in), and
  past slow_trip_seconds that room is logged at once and announced, with how many trips to it have
  been slow. "ok" = it came in time, "slow" = it ran past that, "never" = you left that room with
  it still missing, "longest" = the longest wait there. File: data/<game>/<Char>/mdemon_rooms.yaml,
  keyed by room id (with the room title and the date of the last event).
  It sends none at all while you stand in one of quiet_rooms (the locker vaults, the pawnshops,
  the Mist Harbor Firefly Villa merchant lounge and the Wayside Inn dining room, where
  Dreavenings are held; edit the list in the method).
=end

require "yaml"
require "fileutils"

module MdemonRefresh
  # === config (edit to taste) ===================================================
  MINOR_SUMMONING_SPELL   = "Minor Summoning"
  REFRESH_THRESHOLD_MINUTES = 10
  CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS  = 15
  SEND_MANA_AT            = 40   # resting with at least this much mana -> fill the demon (;demonmana)
  CALL_GAP_SECONDS         = 15  # demon missing from the room: order it back this often
  CALL_BLOCKED_GAP_SECONDS = 90  # ...but this rarely where the game says the magic interferes
  TOWN_ON_AFTER_MINUTES    = 3   # still "on its way" after this long in a legal town: TELL MDEMON TO TOWN ON
  STUCK_WARN_MINUTES       = 10  # still "on its way" after this long: say once that it may be lost
  RETURN_REPLY = /already here!|acknowledges your order|interfering with your|You have no minor demon at this time/i
  DEMON_LINK   = %r{(?:[Bb]ut your|Your|your) <pushBold/><a exist="(\d+)" noun="([\w,'-]+)">([\w\-' ]+)</a><popBold/>}
  # No vakra runestone left: true = fuse a new one with fizzfuse (a bank + general store + alchemist trip,
  # then it walks back). With FUSE_ONLY_WHEN_RESTING_IN_TOWN it never starts that
  # mid-hunt -- it waits until you're resting in town. false = ask you to NOD first.
  AUTO_FUSE_RUNESTONE     = true
  FUSE_ONLY_WHEN_RESTING_IN_TOWN = true

  # === helpers ===================================================================
  def self.rummage_and_rub
    held_item_id = checkleft ? GameObj.left_hand.id : nil

    if held_item_id
      fput "stow left"
      waitrt?
    end

    result = Lich::Util.issue_command(
      "rumm in my kit for runestone vakra",
      /drawn on it|can't seem to locate/,
      include_end: false, quiet: true, silent: true
    ).last.to_s

    return :missing if result =~ /can't seem to locate/

    waitrt?
    # A stone fused from a general-store smooth stone has the noun "stone", not
    # "runestone" (2026-11-11), so address the item by id rather than by noun.
    stone = nil
    30.times {
      stone = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].compact.find { |o| o.id.to_s =~ /\A\d+\z/ && o.noun =~ /stone/ }
      break if stone
      sleep 0.1
    }
    ref = stone ? "##{stone.id}" : "my runestone"
    fput "rub #{ref}"
    waitrt?
    fput "put #{ref} in my kit"
    :ok
  ensure
    if held_item_id
      fput "get ##{held_item_id}"
      waitrt?
    end
  end

  # Rooms where the demon is never called back (Scott 11/13): standing at the locker or in a
  # Dreavening you don't want `tell mdemon return` going out every 15 s. Room ids as the map
  # prints them: 15948 the Landing locker vault and 35474 the Icemule one (where `go2 locker`
  # ends up, per the logs), 3619 Wayside Inn, Dining Room (where ;dreavening sits you). The
  # pawnshops too (Scott 11/14): 408 Kilron's Pawnshop, Front Room in the Landing and 2464 Pawnshop,
  # Interior in Icemule, where `go2 pawnshop` ends up. And 16338 Firefly Villa, Merchant Lounge in
  # Mist Harbor (Scott 11/15). A METHOD so an edit applies the next time the script starts.
  def self.quiet_rooms
    [15948, 35474, 3619, 408, 2464, 16338]
  end

  # What the progress lines compare a trip with (see the header). METHODS, not constants, so an
  # edit applies the next time the script starts.
  def self.normal_trip_seconds
    15
  end

  def self.slow_trip_seconds
    60
  end

  def self.demon_label
    @demon_name ? "Your #{@demon_name}" : "Your demon"
  end

  # Every order for the first minute (orders 1-5, 15 s apart), then one a minute (9, 13, ...):
  # how long the trip has taken so far.
  def self.report_trip_progress(now)
    n = @orders_this_trip.to_i
    return unless n <= 5 || (n % 4) == 1
    secs = (now - @away_since).round
    if n == 1
      echo "#{demon_label} wasn't here -- ordered it back (a normal trip takes about #{normal_trip_seconds} s)."
    elsif secs >= slow_trip_seconds
      echo "#{demon_label} is slow: #{secs} s and #{n} orders so far (normal is about #{normal_trip_seconds} s; the game gives no ETA)."
    else
      echo "#{demon_label} is still on its way: #{secs} s, order ##{n} (normal is about #{normal_trip_seconds} s)."
    end
  end

  # The trip is over. When the demon arrived, say how long it took, once.
  def self.trip_over(now, arrived)
    if arrived && @away_since
      n = @orders_this_trip.to_i
      echo "#{demon_label} is back after #{(now - @away_since).round} s (#{n} order#{n == 1 ? '' : 's'})."
      waited = now - [@away_since, @room_since.to_f].max
      record_room(Room.current&.id.to_i, @slow_logged ? :late : :ok, waited)
    end
    @away_since = nil
    @orders_this_trip = 0
    @slow_logged = false
  end

  # Every second from the main loop: the moment a demon we sent for shows up, say so.
  def self.note_arrival
    return unless @away_since && demon_here?
    trip_over(Time.now.to_f, true)
    @town_on_tried = false
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "note_arrival: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
  end

  # --- rooms where the demon is slow or never shows up (Scott 11/20) -------------------------
  # The wait is counted per room: from the first order, or from the moment you walked in if that
  # was later. Past slow_trip_seconds in one room it is logged at once (so a demon that never comes
  # is still on record); the other outcomes are "ok" (came in time), "late" (came after being
  # logged slow, only the longest wait is updated) and "never" (you left that room with it still
  # missing). Kept in data/<game>/<Char>/mdemon_rooms.yaml, keyed by room id.
  def self.rooms_file
    File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, "mdemon_rooms.yaml")
  end

  def self.load_room_stats
    return {} unless File.exist?(rooms_file)
    data = YAML.safe_load(File.read(rooms_file))
    data.is_a?(Hash) ? data : {}
  rescue StandardError
    {}
  end

  def self.room_title(id)
    t = Room[id]&.title
    t = t.first if t.respond_to?(:first)
    t.to_s.delete("[]").strip
  rescue StandardError
    ""
  end

  # event: :ok, :slow, :late or :never (see above). waited = seconds spent waiting in that room.
  def self.record_room(id, event, waited)
    return if id.to_i.zero?
    data = load_room_stats
    rec = (data[id.to_i] ||= {})
    %w[ok slow never longest].each { |k| rec[k] = rec[k].to_i }
    rec["title"] = room_title(id)
    case event
    when :ok    then rec["ok"] += 1
    when :slow  then rec["slow"] += 1
    when :never then rec["never"] += 1
    end
    rec["longest"] = [rec["longest"], waited.round].max
    rec["last"] = Time.now.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M")
    FileUtils.mkdir_p(File.dirname(rooms_file))
    tmp = "#{rooms_file}.tmp"
    File.write(tmp, data.to_yaml)
    File.rename(tmp, rooms_file)
    if event == :slow
      echo "#{rec['title']} (room #{id}): the demon is past #{slow_trip_seconds} s here -- slow #{rec['slow']} of #{rec['ok'] + rec['slow']} trips to this room so far, longest #{rec['longest']} s (saved to mdemon_rooms.yaml)."
    elsif event == :never
      echo "You left #{rec['title']} (room #{id}) with the demon still missing after #{waited.round} s there (#{rec['never']} time#{rec['never'] == 1 ? '' : 's'} now)."
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "record_room: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
  end

  # Every second: keep the current room, and when a trip passes slow_trip_seconds in the room you
  # are standing in, put that room on record.
  def self.track_room
    now = Time.now.to_f
    id = Room.current&.id.to_i
    return if id.zero?
    if id != @room_id
      if @room_id && @away_since && @slow_logged
        record_room(@room_id, :never, @room_seen_at.to_f - [@away_since, @room_since.to_f].max)
      end
      @slow_logged = false
      @room_id = id
      @room_since = now
    end
    @room_seen_at = now
    return unless @away_since && !@slow_logged
    waited = now - [@away_since, @room_since.to_f].max
    return if waited < slow_trip_seconds
    @slow_logged = true
    record_room(id, :slow, waited)
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "track_room: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
  end

  def self.demon_here?
    return false unless @demon_id
    Array(GameObj.npcs).any? { |n| n && n.id.to_s == @demon_id.to_s }
  end

  # `tell mdemon return` when the demon isn't in the room (see the header). The first call
  # also learns the demon's id from the reply, whatever illusion it is wearing.
  def self.call_demon_back
    unless Effects::Spells.active?(MINOR_SUMMONING_SPELL)
      @away_since = nil   # no demon any more: a later one must not inherit this trip's clock
      @orders_this_trip = 0
      @slow_logged = false
      return
    end
    return if checkdead || checkstunned
    return if quiet_rooms.include?(Room.current&.id.to_i)
    now = Time.now.to_f
    # The "interfering" slow-down belongs to the room that said it; walk out and ask again at once.
    @call_blocked = false unless @blocked_room == XMLData.room_id
    return if now - @last_call.to_f < (@call_blocked ? CALL_BLOCKED_GAP_SECONDS : CALL_GAP_SECONDS)
    if demon_here?
      trip_over(now, true)
      @town_on_tried = false
      return
    end
    @last_call = now
    text = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("tell mdemon return", RETURN_REPLY).to_a.join("\n")
    if text =~ DEMON_LINK
      @demon_id = Regexp.last_match(1)
      @demon_name = Regexp.last_match(3)
    end
    @call_blocked = text =~ /interfering with your/i ? true : false
    @blocked_room = @call_blocked ? XMLData.room_id : nil
    if text =~ /acknowledges your order/i
      @away_since ||= now
      @orders_this_trip = @orders_this_trip.to_i + 1
      report_trip_progress(now)
      town_on_if_stuck(now, text)
      warn_if_stuck(now, text)
    elsif text =~ /already here!/i
      trip_over(now, true)
      @town_on_tried = false
    elsif text =~ /You have no minor demon/i
      trip_over(now, false)
      @town_on_tried = false
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "call_demon_back: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
  end

  # gswiki Minor Summoning (725): minor demons are legal in Wehnimer's Landing, Icemule Trace and
  # Mist Harbor (the Isle of Four Winds on the map); in other towns they fall under justice.
  def self.demons_legal_here?
    room = Room.current
    return false unless room
    town = Room[room.find_nearest_by_tag("town")]
    !!(town && town.location.to_s =~ /Wehnimer's Landing|Icemule Trace|Isle of Four Winds|Mist Harbor/i)
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  # 11/04-05: with TOWN OFF (the default) a demon with no illusion won't enter a town on its own,
  # only while following you, so once go2 outran the grantris in Wehnimer's Landing every order
  # "began to travel" for half an hour and nothing came (Rolfard on Discord; gswiki). The verlok
  # that "passed fine" was disguised as a raven. Verified reply:
  #   >tell mdemon to town on
  #   Your verlok'asha will enter town without an illusion.
  # Once per absence looks at where you are; once per demon it actually says it.
  def self.town_on_if_stuck(now, text)
    return if @town_on_tried || now - @away_since < TOWN_ON_AFTER_MINUTES * 60
    @town_on_tried = true
    return if @demon_id && @town_on_id == @demon_id
    return unless demons_legal_here?
    @town_on_id = @demon_id
    name = text =~ DEMON_LINK ? Regexp.last_match(3) : "demon"
    echo "Your #{name} has been on its way #{TOWN_ON_AFTER_MINUTES}+ minutes. Telling it TOWN ON (a demon with no illusion won't walk into town by itself)."
    fput "tell mdemon to town on"
  end

  # Still "on its way" after STUCK_WARN_MINUTES (11/04-05: the grantris, about half an hour of
  # logged-in time before TOWN ON was known). Say so once per absence (time counts only while
  # this script runs, so mostly logged in).
  def self.warn_if_stuck(now, text)
    if now - @away_since < STUCK_WARN_MINUTES * 60
      @stuck_warned = false
      return
    end
    return if @stuck_warned
    @stuck_warned = true
    name = text =~ DEMON_LINK ? Regexp.last_match(3) : "demon"
    type = name.split.last.to_s.split("'").first.to_s.downcase
    # an igaesha's noun is "smoke", "fog", ...; a disguised demon's is "weasel", "gnoll", ...
    type = "<type>" unless %w[grik imp abyran grantris igaesha verlok aishan shien arashan].include?(type)
    _respond "<pushBold/>[mdemon_refresh] Your #{name} has been on its way for #{STUCK_WARN_MINUTES}+ minutes and hasn't arrived; it may be stuck. ;summond #{type} offers to send it back and summon a new one.<popBold/>"
  end

  # Once per rest, as soon as there's mana to spare (the send costs ~30 and the rest
  # regens it, so the demon's store is free; sending at the end of a rest isn't).
  def self.store_mana_while_resting
    unless checksitting
      @mana_stored = false
      return
    end
    return if @mana_stored || Char.mana < SEND_MANA_AT
    return unless Effects::Spells.active?(MINOR_SUMMONING_SPELL)
    return if GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
    @mana_stored = true
    Script.run("demonmana", "send")
  end

  # No built-in "in town": compare this room's location with the one bigshot rests in
  # (UserVars.op["resting_room_id"]); false when it isn't configured.
  def self.in_town?
    id = (UserVars.op.is_a?(Hash) ? UserVars.op["resting_room_id"].to_s.strip : "")
    return false if id.empty?
    resting = Room.list[id.to_i]
    !!(resting && Room.current.location == resting.location)
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  def self.safe_to_fuse?
    return true unless FUSE_ONLY_WHEN_RESTING_IN_TOWN
    in_town? && checksitting && GameObj.targets.none? { |t| t && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
  end

  # fizzfuse walks around town; bigshot's rest loop shouldn't also decide to walk.
  def self.with_bigshot_paused
    paused = Script.running?("bigshot") && !Script.paused?("bigshot") && Script.pause("bigshot")
    yield
  ensure
    Script.unpause("bigshot") if paused
  end

  def self.wait_for_nod
    echo "Type 'nod' when you're ready to let fizzfuse fuse a new vakra runestone."
    loop do
      line = get
      break if line =~ /^You nod/i
    end
  end

  def self.attempt_refresh
    status = rummage_and_rub
    return :ok if status == :ok

    if AUTO_FUSE_RUNESTONE
      return :wait unless safe_to_fuse?
      echo "No vakra runestone in kit -- fusing a new one (resting in town)."
    else
      echo "No vakra runestone in kit -- fusing one via fizzfuse will pull you away from the hunt."
      wait_for_nod
    end

    with_bigshot_paused { Script.run("fizzfuse", "rune vakra") }
    rummage_and_rub
  end

  # === main ======================================================================
  def self.run
    # module state survives between runs (Lich re-opens the module)
    @away_since = nil
    @orders_this_trip = 0
    @slow_logged = false
    @room_id = nil
    @room_since = nil
    @room_seen_at = nil
    @stuck_warned = false
    @town_on_tried = false
    @call_blocked = false
    @blocked_room = nil
    echo "MdemonRefresh started! Watching Minor Summoning (refresh buffer: #{REFRESH_THRESHOLD_MINUTES} min)."
    echo "Auto-fuse runestone: #{AUTO_FUSE_RUNESTONE}"
    echo "Stop with ;kill mdemon_refresh"

    loop do
      if Effects::Spells.active?(MINOR_SUMMONING_SPELL)
        remaining = Effects::Spells.time_left(MINOR_SUMMONING_SPELL)
        @waiting = false if remaining >= REFRESH_THRESHOLD_MINUTES

        # waiting for town: don't rummage the kit every 15s mid-hunt, just look again
        # once it's safe to fuse
        if remaining < REFRESH_THRESHOLD_MINUTES && (!@waiting || safe_to_fuse?)
          echo "Minor Summoning has #{remaining.round(1)} minutes left, refreshing demon."
          result = attempt_refresh
          was_waiting = @waiting
          @waiting = (result == :wait)

          if result == :ok
            echo "Demon refreshed."
          elsif result == :wait
            echo "No vakra runestone -- will fuse one when you're resting in town." unless was_waiting
          else
            echo "Could not refresh demon -- still no vakra runestone available."
          end
        end
      else
        @waiting = false
      end

      store_mana_while_resting
      call_demon_back
      CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS.times do
        sleep 1
        track_room
        note_arrival
      end
    end
  end
end

MdemonRefresh.run
